---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FaqSection from '../components/FaqSection.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How It Works – Background Changer & Photo Background Editor"
  description="Learn how Background Changer isolates subjects in-browser, customizes colors, crops to official passport and job dimensions, and exports high-quality photos."
  canonicalPath="/how-it-works"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/60 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-3 border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-900">
        Step-by-Step Guide
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        How Background Changer Works
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 max-w-xl mx-auto">
        Fast, private, client-side <strong>photo background editor</strong> designed specifically for <strong>job application photo</strong>, <strong>passport photo background</strong>, and <strong>ID photo background changer</strong> requirements.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Step by Step Guides -->
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">
            01
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            Client-Side AI Background Remover
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          When you upload an image to our <strong>image background changer</strong>, our client-side neural network analyzes the photo layers entirely within your browser's WebAssembly sandbox. It acts as an instant <strong>background remover</strong>, isolating the subject and creating an alpha transparency mask without ever transferring your photo to a remote server.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">
            02
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            Non-Destructive Composite Layering & Photo Editor Online
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Unlike standard image compressors that repeatedly degrade pixel quality with every adjustment, our <strong>photo editor online</strong> keeps your original high-resolution subject intact through non-destructive canvas layering:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 font-mono text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-1">
          <div>Original Source Image (High-Resolution In-Memory)</div>
          <div class="text-blue-500">↳ Alpha Transparency Subject Layer (Isolated Foreground)</div>
          <div class="text-emerald-500">↳ Background Layer (Solid White, Blue, Custom HEX/RGB, or Custom Uploaded Image)</div>
          <div class="text-amber-500">↳ Aspect Ratio Crop & Rotation Matrix (1:1, 3:4, 2×2 in)</div>
          <div class="text-purple-500">↳ Non-destructive Color Grading (Brightness, Contrast, Sharpness, Exposure)</div>
          <div>↳ Final Resampled Export (JPG, PNG, WebP)</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 shadow-sm">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">
            03
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            Official Guidelines for Passport & Job Application Photo Background
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Government agencies, embassy visa portals, and corporate HR departments enforce strict document photo standards:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          <li><strong>Background color:</strong> Usually a clean <strong>white background photo</strong> or neutral off-white (or light <strong>blue background photo</strong> for specific regional ID cards).</li>
          <li><strong>Dimensions & Aspect Ratio:</strong> Standard US passports require 2×2 inches (600×600 px at 300 DPI) with a 1:1 square ratio. Standard resume/CV portals typically use 3:4 vertical portraits.</li>
          <li><strong>Subject Head Positioning:</strong> The head (from crown to chin) should occupy between 50% and 69% of the total image height. Use our built-in <em>Face Guide</em> overlay to align your portrait effortlessly.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-4 p-3 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-900/60 text-xs text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200">
          <strong>Important Disclaimer:</strong> Exact requirements vary by organization and country. Always check your application's official specifications before final submission.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA button -->
    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-3.5 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold text-sm shadow-md shadow-blue-500/20 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]"
      >
        <span>Open Background Changer Now</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line>
          <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"></polyline>
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <FaqSection />
</Layout>
